            {
                id selecttwo
                title "Reconsider the two-entity select surface from core principles"
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-06T13:02:24.600154Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Operator directive (2026-09-06): \"The entire principle of SelectTwo needs to be considered from core principles because a lot of these APIs are hacky nonsense.\" Trigger: the joined-decode work exposed SelectTwo::into_partial_model / stream_partial_model as pre-existingly broken (M::select_cols adds bare field names, decode reads A_/B_ prefixes — untested anywhere), and the surface accreted piecemeal: SelectTwo vs SelectTwoMany vs SelectTwoProjected, find_also_related vs find_with_related vs find_also_linked, the A_/B_ prefix convention, consolidate_query_result regroup, per-variant cursor_by shims, and the pipeline now offering a principled alternative for multi-relation reads. Deliverable: a design spike on a branch (spike/selecttwo) — inventory the surface and its real uses, evaluate against the fork's doctrines (unrepresentable invalid states, one vocabulary with the pipeline, no decode ambiguity), and return a verdict: redesign shape, deletions, and what the partial-model story should be. No production code lands from the spike; implementing nodes get boarded from the verdict."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-06T13:15:01.024306Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Spike verdict (4/4 probes conclusive, live-tested; artifacts on spike/selecttwo): THE PAIR-READ DESERVES TO EXIST; THE PAIR-PROJECTION MACHINERY DOES NOT. Keep unchanged: SelectTwo, find_also_related/linked, select_also, one/all/stream, decode-only into_model<M,N>, the sound keyset cursors + paginator. Delete outright: SelectTwoMany (+4 trait impls; its injected ORDER BY silently precedes and overrides caller ordering — probe 4), find_with_related/linked, select_with, SelectTwoCustom/SelectTwoProjected (prefix convention leaked into user space), SelectTwo::select_only/select (makes hand-matched pair projections UNREPRESENTABLE), SelectTwo::into_partial_model + stream_partial_model (probes 1-2: renders bare colliding columns, decode reads never-rendered A_/B_ — fails on EVERY row; zero call sites, zero tests: has never worked for anyone), consolidate_query_result_of_ordered_rows (dead). Replace: 10-line SelectTwo::all_grouped terminal (probe 4 reproduces SelectTwoMany::all exactly AND lets caller ordering dominate — a fix); one internal append_b_columns writer replacing 4 copies (combine.rs, join.rs ×2, loader.rs). Partial-pair story: deleted now; if demanded later, select_cols_pre(pre) is proven sound by probe 3. Pipeline CANNOT absorb the pair-read (prqlc renames colliding outputs to _expr_N; whole-side absence semantics need the witness machinery). Migration: 21 mechanical test-site moves, 0 for the partial deletions. Node sequence: all-grouped → delete-selecttwomany → delete-projected-pair → b-columns-single-writer (+optional partial-pair-prefix). ~7 spec rules affected (combine, consolidate, modifiers, stream, cursor trims). AWAITING OPERATOR RULING before boarding implementing nodes."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-06T13:22:41.722106Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Operator ruling (2026-09-06) on the spike verdict: REJECTED as too conservative. Verbatim: \"the find_also_related and _linked are bizarre as it is, and don't work particularly well for proper joins. I want a radical rethink here.\" The keep-list (find_also_related/linked, the pair-read core) is NOT ratified; the deletion list stands unopposed but implementing nodes are HELD — a radical redesign of the whole relational-read story may subsume them. Second spike commissioned (spike/relational-read): design the relational-read surface from scratch — N-entity join graphs, join-type control, typed multi-model decode, unification with the pipeline's vocabulary — with the first spike's inventory as ground truth and its probes as evidence the decode witness machinery and auto-prefixing are sound building blocks."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-06T13:42:40.839602Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Spike 2 verdict (spike/relational-read; 4 unit + 5 live probes + 2 compile_fail proofs, all green): BUILD THE N-ARY SOURCE GRAPH; DELETE THE ENTIRE PAIR SURFACE INCLUDING SPIKE 1'S KEEP-LIST. SelectGraph<E, Slots>: root + typed slot list in join order; join type derived from the slot kind (join_maybe → LEFT → Option<Model> via the untouched absence witness; join_one → INNER → bare Model — no Option to unwrap for a join that cannot miss); via() joins-without-decoding (junctions, chain hops); join_maybe_as for the same table twice with caller-bound alias tokens + call-site ON predicates; one projection writer (s{i}_ prefixes, select_as discipline) replacing the FOUR aliasing copies; projection editing and slot mismatch unrepresentable (compile_fail proven). all/one_opt/stream/paginate via ordinary Selector; all_grouped fixes the caller-ordering override. CURSORS DO NOT MOVE — the existing Cursor machinery hosts the graph unchanged (live-proven with after_with resume + NULL tiebreaks); only SelectTwo's entry points re-home. Pipeline gets select_sources((E1, E2.named(t))) as the complement for row-shaped reads (dissolves _expr_N via controlled projection; aggregates-beside-models and right/full joins live there); pipeline-as-sole-surface rejected on cursor evidence; include-tree and full minimalism rejected with numbers (~101 call sites incl. the joined-cursor block would die homeless). Loader stays; load_many_via rewrites internally onto the graph. Kill-list: SelectTwo/Many/Custom/Projected/Model, select_also/with, find_also/with_related, find_also/with_linked, apply_alias, prepare_select_two, SelectA/B, both consolidates, pair partials. Migration ~101 mechanical sites in 9 test files. Node sequence: graph-core → {graph-cursor, graph-grouped, loader-on-graph, pipeline-select-sources} → pair-surface-deletion → linked-fold (optional). Bonus finding to spec: authored on_condition closures that ignore their right param silently misqualify under aliases. AWAITING OPERATOR RULING."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-06T14:08:53.465041Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @decision
                        text "Operator ruling (2026-09-06): ADOPTED — \"spec it up and then opus subagents for implementation.\" The SelectGraph verdict stands as reported: N-ary typed source graph with join type derived from the slot kind, one projection writer under s{i}_ prefixes, the untouched absence witness as decoder, cursors re-homed with machinery unchanged, pipeline select_sources as the row-shaped complement, loader retained and internally rewritten, the full inherited pair surface deleted. Boarded as the graph tree: spec → core → {cursor, grouped, loader, pipeline-sources} → pair-deletion → linked-fold. Spec authored first; implementing nodes claim the new rules after they land."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-06T14:08:58.856007Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Done (nplan complete)"
                    }
                )
