                        at 2026-09-03T18:36:40.532368Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Operator: \"DbErr should just be Error\" — the Err-suffixed family predates the fork and reads as SeaORM, not Rust. DbErr -> Error (crate root export), RuntimeErr -> RuntimeError, ColumnFromStrErr -> ColumnFromStrError, SqlErr -> SqlError; pgorm-query's ValueTupleErr -> ValueTupleError. Variant TryIntoErr -> a non-redundant name (Error::TryIntoErr reads stuttery). Add the idiomatic pub type Result<T, E = Error> alias at the crate root. Renames are outright per delete-don't-deprecate: no aliases left behind. Macros generate paths naming the old types — sweep pgorm-macros' quote! bodies. Every spec rule body naming DbErr changes and therefore bumps + re-pins (error.model family normatively; count the prose mentions across docs/spec first)."
                    }

