                        text "Operator addition (2026-09-04, mid-flight): stringly out(\"rn\") at every reference site is the wrong shape — the alias should be a value with ONE definition site. Add an alias token: let rn = alias(\"rn\"); a Copy newtype over the name that (a) declares via .as_(rn) — as_ accepts impl Into<AliasName> so bare &str stays legal for one-shot aliases nobody references — and (b) references by behaving as an expression itself (token implements the comparison/sort surface or Into<Expr> as an unqualified ident), so filter(rn.lte(2)) replaces filter(out(\"rn\").lte(2)). out() as a public constructor should disappear from the fluent surface if the token covers it (judgment: keep a low-level escape or delete outright per delete-don't-deprecate). Honest ceiling stands: an unattached token still compiles and the server catches it — state that in the rule; do not build brand machinery to tie tokens to attachment (overkill, operator not asked for it). Update the five before/after pairs and pipeline.surface accordingly."
