                        text "Security review 2026-09-08, severity P1. inject_parameters replaces $N textually wherever it appears — inside block comments and dollar-quoted bodies included — so a value can escape its context: \"SELECT $1::text AS value /* $1 */\" with a payload ending the comment and appending UNION ALL SELECT executed the payload (probe inline_parameters_preserve_block_comments); a $$-quoted source similarly executed part of the value (inline_parameters_preserve_dollar_quoted_bodies). Fix: substitution must be lexer-aware — the pg_query tokenizer (sql.token, already the paginator's and census's oracle) yields PARAM tokens with spans; replace exactly those and nothing else, so $N spellings inside comments, strings and dollar-quotes are inert text. The substituted literal itself renders through the (separately fixed) inline string escaper. SPEC IMPACT: bump sql.render.inject to state token-level substitution and its oracle."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-08T09:44:03.125508Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                    }

