            {
                id raw-identifier-casts
                title "Function and type names render as quoted identifiers, never raw SQL"
                kind @fix
                sealed true
                log (
                    {
                        at 2026-09-08T09:15:19.922093Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Security review 2026-09-08, severity P1, the widest node. Function names (Func::cust), cast targets (cast_as via Func::cast_as's Expr::cust of the iden text, and as_enum's rewrite through it), and enum type names in DDL (prepare_column_type, enumeration()) are all emitted as RAW text even when passed as Alias identifiers: Func::cust(Alias::new(\"COALESCE(7) + 100 --\")) and cast_as(Alias::new(\"int4) + 100 --\")) both executed injected expressions; enumeration(Alias::new(\"text, injected integer\")) added a column to CREATE TABLE; and the raw convention also case-folds, so as_enum(Alias::new(\"ReviewStatus\")) fails to find \"ReviewStatus\" (probes custom_function_identifier_is_not_sql, cast_type_identifier_is_not_sql, enum_type_identifier_preserves_case, enum_ddl_name_cannot_add_a_column). FIX DIRECTION: type and function names become structured renderings — dot-split parts each quoted per ident-quoting, an optional [] array suffix kept structural — replacing every Expr::cust(iden.to_string()) spelling: Func::cust/cast_as, the AsEnum rewrite, prepare_column_type's Enum arm and the Enum-to-Custom projection, and the schema-qualified compositions from enum-schema-surface (enum_cast_iden's \"schema.name\" string and the \"{name}[]\" Alias hacks become structure). CONSEQUENCES: golden SQL changes everywhere casts render (CAST('x' AS tea) → CAST('x' AS \"tea\"), text[] → \"text\"[], tenant_a.status → \"tenant_a\".\"status\"); grammar-sugar type spellings that are not catalog names (\"double precision\") stop working via cast_as-by-name — spell the catalog name (float8) or use ColumnType. SPEC IMPACT: bump sql.render.cast-param-type, sql.render.ddl.enum-type, sql.render.ddl.types (if it states raw), entity.traits.column.enum-cast (the documented raw/unquoted cast convention REVERSES to quoted), and reconcile query.graph.writer's cast language plus the pipeline's read-cast probe (source_read_cast matches the AsEnum/Cast shapes — its extraction must follow the new structure)."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-08T09:53:08.788034Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @note
                        text "Design settled (2026-09-08, lead): ONE structured cast representation. (1) pgorm-query types.rs gains TypeName { schema: Option<DynIden>, name: DynIden, array: bool } with a prepare() that renders quoted dot-joined parts plus a structural [] suffix, and a raw_text() giving the old dotted spelling for the pipeline adapter. (2) SimpleExpr::AsEnum becomes AsEnum(Box<TypeName>, Box<SimpleExpr>); Expr::as_enum<T: IntoIden> wraps TypeName::new, as_enum_type takes it whole; Expr::cast_as and SimpleExpr::cast_as build the SAME AsEnum shape (a cast is a cast); Func::cast_as (the FunctionCall-with-Expr::cust spelling) is DELETED and callers rerouted. (3) The renderer's AsEnum arm stops rewriting through cast_as text and renders CAST(operand AS <TypeName>) directly — it MUST replicate sql.render.cast-param-type's pin: a Value operand goes through push_param_source_typed. (4) prepare_column_type's Enum arm and Function::Custom render quoted (function names via iden.prepare, not unquoted). ColumnType::Custom stays raw as the documented escape hatch. (5) ORM: enum_cast_iden becomes enum_type_name -> Option<TypeName>; save_enum_as / save_enum_array_as / select_enum_as build TypeName (Text / TextArray become TypeName::new(Text) / .array() — the \"{name}[]\" Alias string hacks die); graph source_read_cast matches AsEnum(tn, _) and hands the pipeline adapter tn.raw_text() so PRQL behavior is unchanged (pipeline ident safety is pipeline-hostile-identifiers' scope). (6) Golden sweep: every cast rendering gains quotes (AS tea → AS \"tea\", AS tea[] → AS \"tea\"[], AS tenant_a.status → AS \"tenant_a\".\"status\", derive save_as AS text → AS \"text\"); grammar-sugar type spellings (double precision) stop working by name — catalog names or ColumnType. Spec: bump sql.render.cast-param-type, sql.render.ddl.enum-type, entity.traits.column.enum-cast (raw convention reverses to quoted), sql.ast.func (Func::cast_as deletion) and reconcile query.graph.writer's cast sentence. Acceptance: the four probes custom_function_identifier_is_not_sql, cast_type_identifier_is_not_sql, enum_type_identifier_preserves_case, enum_ddl_name_cannot_add_a_column in tests/sql_security_tests.rs (untracked acceptance file, to be committed when all six remaining security tests pass)."
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-08T09:53:15.58423Z
                        author "brendan@necessary.nu"
                        kind @status
                        text "Todo → Doing (nplan start)"
                    }

                    {
                        at 2026-09-08T13:14:34.249448Z
